{"sha":"d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab","node_id":"C_kwDOTg6RstoAKGQyOGMwYzc5ZGZjN2FlY2I5NGM0MGFjYmJjODEwOWVjZWUyNmQyYWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"cyclotron","email":"cyclotron@atomdrift","date":"2026-10-21T20:15:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"cyclotron","email":"cyclotron@atomdrift","date":"2026-10-21T20:16:03Z"},"message":"unconvicted:suspicious: 3 samples, 2 moved, 3 relabeled (S 4→1)\n\n@aimarket-warden-0.18.0.tgz 0% H0 S1 →good 30b96f217c7ca951c3061e33b12e2601a739d6e14384e17f33998dc512f21c73\n  Warden 0.18.0 (MCP firewall): ships public-key pem only, verify-side\ncrucible-logging-0.1.2-alpha.crate 0% H0 S2→0 →good b915084a9424ba9be42359bf581d2fd4ab2dd552b590b3cf1ed07f38fa515952\n  crucible-logging 0.1.2-alpha: ordinary registry logger, name-only FP\nComfyUI_RaykoStudio-0.51.1.zip 0% H0 S1→0 →good 2516fb688ade0bcbd0cfe33816778f12879b43117dac1cc77aa315e8cd8ea99e\n  RaykoStudio ComfyUI nodes: PNG text metadata node, no backdoor\n\nModel: opencode:zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash@high","tree":{"sha":"d746c6fef7c76aaf9b9ab64ebedc74d02deb8f84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/git/trees/d746c6fef7c76aaf9b9ab64ebedc74d02deb8f84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/git/commits/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/commits/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab","html_url":"https://github.com/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/commit/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/commits/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab/comments","author":null,"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"254bc2d6a64bfe6dcad69ca7a1be0ec1442a7d03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/commits/254bc2d6a64bfe6dcad69ca7a1be0ec1442a7d03","html_url":"https://github.com/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/commit/254bc2d6a64bfe6dcad69ca7a1be0ec1442a7d03"}],"stats":{"total":45,"additions":43,"deletions":2},"files":[{"sha":"4de7e8799c8f2e67b3dfaa17c947492036f14f99","filename":"metadata/package/publishing/cargo-registry-manifest.yaml","status":"added","additions":16,"deletions":0,"changes":16,"blob_url":"https://github.com/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/blob/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab/metadata%2Fpackage%2Fpublishing%2Fcargo-registry-manifest.yaml","raw_url":"https://github.com/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/raw/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab/metadata%2Fpackage%2Fpublishing%2Fcargo-registry-manifest.yaml","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/contents/metadata%2Fpackage%2Fpublishing%2Fcargo-registry-manifest.yaml?ref=d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@\n+# Cargo writes this normalization banner into every manifest it generates for\n+# a crates.io upload (the published tarball also carries .cargo_vcs_info.json).\n+# Its presence says the artifact in front of you is a registry release, not a\n+# local working tree or a synthetic fixture tree.\n+defaults:\n+  for: [cargo.toml]\n+  platforms: [unix, windows]\n+  conf: 0.85\n+\n+traits:\n+  - id: cargo-registry-generated-manifest\n+    desc: Cargo manifest generated for registry upload\n+    crit: notable\n+    if:\n+      type: text\n+      substr: THIS FILE IS AUTOMATICALLY GENERATED BY CARGO"},{"sha":"5e4232f06e7a37aeae27de9bc772a58f8b5b1e3a","filename":"objectives/supply-chain/hidden-payload/cargo-behavior/traits.yaml","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":0,"changes":5,"blob_url":"https://github.com/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/blob/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab/objectives%2Fsupply-chain%2Fhidden-payload%2Fcargo-behavior%2Ftraits.yaml","raw_url":"https://github.com/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/raw/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab/objectives%2Fsupply-chain%2Fhidden-payload%2Fcargo-behavior%2Ftraits.yaml","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/contents/objectives%2Fsupply-chain%2Fhidden-payload%2Fcargo-behavior%2Ftraits.yaml?ref=d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab","patch":"@@ -411,6 +411,11 @@ traits:\n     # Oxide's Crucible storage service ships a hakari workspace-hack crate\n     # named after the project, which is not a synthetic scenario.\n     - id: metadata/package/workspace::published-workspace-hack\n+    # A crates.io release is the published artifact, not a local synthetic\n+    # scenario tree: registry-generated manifests (the normalization banner\n+    # every uploaded crate carries) mark real packages like crucible-logging,\n+    # an ordinary logger whose name merely contains the fixture root's word.\n+    - id: metadata/package/publishing::cargo-registry-generated-manifest\n - id: cargo-path-crucible-technique-a\n   desc: Cargo crucible behavior keyword\n   crit: suspicious"},{"sha":"3470965281c683dff59bf659cc669da59ff7ff9b","filename":"well-known/malware/botnet/comfyui/traits.yaml","status":"modified","additions":22,"deletions":2,"changes":24,"blob_url":"https://github.com/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/blob/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab/well-known%2Fmalware%2Fbotnet%2Fcomfyui%2Ftraits.yaml","raw_url":"https://github.com/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/raw/d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab/well-known%2Fmalware%2Fbotnet%2Fcomfyui%2Ftraits.yaml","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isotope13-dev/traits-dev/contents/well-known%2Fmalware%2Fbotnet%2Fcomfyui%2Ftraits.yaml?ref=d28c0c79dfc7aecb94c40acbbc8109ecee26d2ab","patch":"@@ -42,12 +42,32 @@ traits:\n   if:\n     type: string_literal\n     substr: 77.110.96.200\n-- id: comfyui-torch-masquerade\n-  desc: ComfyUI backdoor masquerading as image tensor\n+- id: comfyui-dummy-tensor-fallback\n+  desc: Zero-tensor error fallback in a ComfyUI node\n+  crit: component\n+  conf: 0.9\n   if:\n     type: text\n     substr: dummy_img = torch.zeros\n composite_rules:\n+# The campaign backdoor node's code poses as benign tensor handling (the\n+# zero-tensor error fallback above) while carrying a payload mechanism. The\n+# fallback idiom alone is common in honest nodes -- dozens spell their error\n+# fallback exactly this way -- so the masquerade finding requires payload\n+# machinery in the same file: deserialization, a remote fetch, or the\n+# campaign's own staging/C2 markers.\n+- id: comfyui-torch-masquerade\n+  desc: ComfyUI backdoor masquerading as image tensor\n+  all:\n+  - id: comfyui-dummy-tensor-fallback\n+  any:\n+  - id: micro-behaviors/data/serialize/unsafe::pickle-loads\n+  - id: micro-behaviors/data/serialize/unsafe::pickle-load\n+  - id: micro-behaviors/data/serialize/unsafe::marshal-loads-symbol\n+  - id: micro-behaviors/communications/http/request/client::urllib-url-literal\n+  - id: objectives/command-and-control/dropper/compat::cross-platform-git-bash-exe\n+  - id: comfyui-perf-monitor-init\n+  - id: comfyui-c2-ip\n - id: comfyui-six-hour-sleep-reference\n   desc: ComfyUI context with six-hour sleep\n   crit: suspicious"}]}